<!--
  Generated by feature/accent-themes/palette.py — do not hand-edit.

  One accent theme is a pair of overlays: the dark style carries all nine roles, its
  .Light child overrides the six that differ by mode. Which one is applied is decided by
  Prefs.accentOverlay(context, light) — the themes that read these roles cannot branch on
  the mode themselves, and a values-night/ qualifier would follow the *system* while a
  dialog here follows the appearance pref.

  ink / onInk / skip do not change with the mode: the ink is read over video, which is
  dark whatever the pref says. fill is the ink again in dark mode and the theme's own
  light tone in light mode — for 31 hues no single fill clears 3:1 on white and on a dark
  ground at once.

  The values and the arithmetic behind them come from mpvEx AppTheme.kt (primaryLight and
  primaryDark, backgroundLight and backgroundDark, and its own scheme formulas); the
  corrections, the gates and the skip hues from feature/material-design/THEMES.md.
-->
